The legacy fixed-size cluster mentioned in
`buildbarn-remote-execution-setup.md` lives separately from the
ondemand work covered here. Inventory it once for reference:

| Role | Hostname | Public IP (fill in) | Private IP (fill in) |
|---|---|---|---|
| central | `____________________` | `____________________` | `____________________` |
| worker-1 | `____________________` | `____________________` | `____________________` |
| worker-2 | `____________________` | `____________________` | `____________________` |

(The ondemand cluster doesn't have a fixed worker IP table — those VMs
are spawned/destroyed by the scaler and addressed by name only.)

## 5. GitHub OAuth App

| Placeholder | Live value (fill in) | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `${GITHUB_OAUTH_APP_NAME}` | `____________________` | App display name shown on the GitHub login page. Currently a personal app; the swap to a Percona-org app is documented in `buildbarn-auth-tls-plan.md` §"Migration Path". |
| `${GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID}` | `(in .env only)`     | Format: `Iv1.<16hex>` or `Ov23li<random>`. |
| `${GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET}` | `(in .env only)` | Generated once on the GitHub side; if rotated, edit `.env` and `docker compose restart dex`. |
| `${GITHUB_TEAM_SLUGS}` | `percona/build-engineers, percona/iit, percona/dev-psmdb` | Lives in `compose/dex/dex.yaml::connectors[].config.orgs[].teams`. Removing a team rejects its members at next OIDC refresh. |

## 6. OIDC / cookie secrets

These are generated locally by `create-central.sh::bake_env()`
the first time it runs (`openssl rand -hex 32`). Store the generated
values in `.env` only — they're only valid against this specific
Dex instance and don't need backing up; if you lose them, regenerate
and restart Dex + bb-browser + bb-scheduler.

| Placeholder | Live value (fill in) |
|---|---|
| `${BB_BROWSER_OIDC_SECRET}` | `(in .env only)` |
| `${BB_SCHED_OIDC_SECRET}` | `(in .env only)` |
| `${BB_PORTAL_OIDC_SECRET}` | `(in .env only)` |
| `${BB_BROWSER_COOKIE_SEED}` | `(in .env only)` |
| `${BB_SCHED_COOKIE_SEED}` | `(in .env only)` |
| `${BB_PORTAL_COOKIE_SEED}` | `(in .env only)` |
| `${BB_PORTAL_DB_PASSWORD}` | `(in .env only)` — bb-portal-backend → bb-portal-db Postgres password. Generated by bake_env, embedded into the rendered `bb-portal.jsonnet::connectionString` and passed as `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` to the bb-portal-db container. |

Effects of rotating each:
- OIDC secrets: re-register with Dex (auto on restart). Active sessions keep working.
- Cookie seeds: every active UI session is invalidated; users get
  bounced through Dex on their next request. Use this if you suspect
  a session-cookie compromise.
- `${BB_PORTAL_DB_PASSWORD}`: rotation requires both bb-portal-db AND
  bb-portal-backend to restart with the new value (the password is
  *also* the postgres superuser password — a stale connection string
  on the backend gives `pq: password authentication failed` until
  the next deploy).

## 7. TLS certificates

Lives at `/etc/buildbarn/certs/{fullchain,privkey}.pem` on the central
host (mode 0644 fullchain, 0640 privkey, both root:root). Bind-mounted
read-only into bb-browser, bb-scheduler-admin, bb-portal-backend, dex,
envoy-proxy.

| Placeholder | Live value (fill in) | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Cert subject (CN/SAN) | `____________________` | Should equal `${PUBLIC_HOSTNAME}` |
| Issuer | Let's Encrypt (R3 or successor) | |
| Key type | ECDSA P-256 | (`certbot --key-type ecdsa --elliptic-curve secp256r1`) |
| Renewal hook | `/etc/letsencrypt/renewal-hooks/deploy/buildbarn.sh` | Copies new cert into `/var/lib/buildbarn/certs/` and `docker compose kill -s SIGHUP envoy-proxy dex bb-browser bb-scheduler-admin` |
| Next expiry | `____________________` | `openssl x509 -in fullchain.pem -noout -enddate` |

